/-!
# Kernel smoke test for graph keys

Decoding, canonicalization and packing of all `231` rows of the first coefficient table
(the multiplier polynomials `f, U, K, M, P`), checked by kernel reduction (`decide +kernel`).
A row is `(rank, number of digits, word, coefficient numerator)`; leading zeros of the decimal
word are restored from the number of digits. The expected lists are packed canonical keys with
the coefficient multiplied by the scalar factor of canonicalization.

We also check that `Key.unpack` inverts `Key.pack` on these keys, and one product and
contraction: the full contraction of `q ⊗ q`, where `q_l = X_{lij} A_{ij}`, is the key of `|q|²`.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace OnePhaseDimension.Certificate.Spike

